From 64493a45695a208c18a5fe1235c01e181d027fa2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Verbovoy <ivanverbovoy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:14:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] server: work queued for the Wayland loop's idle is done
 before GLib sleeps

The Wayland loop runs inside GLib's as a source woken by its fd, and its
idle list - wlroots' frame requests and configures among it - was only
worked through when a client had something to read. Queued from GLib's
side, a D-Bus call or a timeout, it waited for the next unrelated message:
a window brought back from the dock on a still screen got its output frame,
and so its first frame, ~260 ms late (restore 290 ms, Calculator drawing
in 12 of them).
---
 src/server.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/server.c b/src/server.c
index 2c1be51..2d64f85 100644
--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -106,6 +106,14 @@ wayland_event_source_prepare (GSource *base,
 
   *timeout = -1;
 
+  /* Work the Wayland loop was given to do when it next goes idle - a frame
+   * asked for, a configure to send - is only done when it runs, and it runs
+   * when its fd has something to read. Given from GLib's side (a D-Bus call,
+   * a timeout), it waited for the next unrelated client message: a window
+   * brought back from the dock on a still screen waited ~260 ms for the
+   * output's frame, and so for its own. */
+  wl_event_loop_dispatch_idle (wl_display_get_event_loop (source->display));
+
   wl_display_flush_clients (source->display);
 
   return FALSE;
